public function jsonOnly() { return response()-&gt;json($this-&gt;rows()); }</code></pre></div>
<div data-panel="django" class="hidden"><pre class="bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="language-python">def _rows():
    return [{&quot;id&quot;: i, &quot;title&quot;: f&quot;Post title {i}&quot;, &quot;views&quot;: i * 7} for i in range(1, 51)]


def json_only(request):
    # compact separators, or the payload is 299 bytes larger than everyone else&#x27;s
    return JsonResponse(_rows(), safe=False, json_dumps_params={&quot;separators&quot;: (&quot;,&quot;, &quot;:&quot;)})</code></pre></div>
<div data-panel="fastapi" class="hidden"><pre class="bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="language-python">def rows():
    return [{&quot;id&quot;: i, &quot;title&quot;: f&quot;Post title {i}&quot;, &quot;views&quot;: i * 7} for i in range(1, 51)]


# Returning a Response directly skips jsonable_encoder — the cost no other
# stack here pays. The default path is the /json-encoded reference row.
@app.get(&quot;/json&quot;)
async def json_only():
    return JSONResponse(rows())


@app.get(&quot;/json-encoded&quot;)
async def json_encoded():
    return rows()</code></pre></div>
<div data-panel="phoenix" class="hidden"><pre class="bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="language-elixir">defp rows do
  Enum.map(1..50, fn i -&gt; %{id: i, title: &quot;Post title #{i}&quot;, views: i * 7} end)
end

def json_only(conn, _params), do: json(conn, rows())</code></pre></div>
</div>
<p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">Framework overhead only &mdash; no database, no template. Soli serves the API response at <strong class="text-white">11.4x Rails' throughput on 12x less CPU</strong>, and at 1.6x Express, the fastest of the others. The CPU column orders the field the same way the throughput does: Soli 26 µs, Express 47, FastAPI 85, Phoenix 140. On a handler this small, the differences are the cost of the request path itself &mdash; routing, the response object, the header set, the write &mdash; and that is exactly what this row isolates.</p>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4">Template &mdash; 50-row HTML table + layout, ~3 KB</h2>
