}</code></pre></div>
<div data-panel="django" class="hidden"><pre class="bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="language-python">def db_template(request):
    return render(request, &quot;posts/list.html&quot;, {&quot;title&quot;: &quot;Posts&quot;, &quot;items&quot;: _db_rows()})</code></pre></div>
<div data-panel="fastapi" class="hidden"><pre class="bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="language-python">@app.get(&quot;/db-template&quot;)
async def db_template(request: Request):
    return templates.TemplateResponse(
        request, &quot;posts/list.html&quot;, {&quot;title&quot;: &quot;Posts&quot;, &quot;items&quot;: await db_rows()}
    )</code></pre></div>
<div data-panel="phoenix" class="hidden"><pre class="bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="language-elixir">def db_template(conn, _params) do
  conn |&gt; bare() |&gt; render(:list, title: &quot;Posts&quot;, items: db_rows())
end</code></pre></div>
</div>
<p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">The Template row's caveat applies here too: with the query cache off, Soli runs the query on every request, but the page rendered from its result can still come out of the response cache, because the result is the same each time. The uncached row therefore measures the database path in full and the render path at its best.</p>
<p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">Soli takes the row with or without its query cache &mdash; <strong class="text-white">4.5x Rails' throughput uncached</strong>, ahead of Phoenix (72,263) and Express (70,143). What the render costs once a query is in the request differs sharply by stack: <strong class="text-white">nothing for Soli</strong> &mdash; its uncached page and its uncached JSON read are the same 112k req/s &mdash; and nothing for Phoenix, whose page is slightly <em>faster</em> than its JSON read, but <strong class="text-white">26% for Express</strong> (94,755 → 70,143) and 45% for Django.</p>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4">Writes &mdash; create, update and delete, one row per request</h2>
<p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">Each of these measures one write per request against an isolated table, reset to exactly its seeded state before every cell so no stack inherits a table another stack grew or emptied. Update and delete address one row by primary key, drawn at random from the whole table in every stack.</p>
<p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong class="text-white">Durability is matched.</strong> SoliDB's writes go through RocksDB's default path &mdash; the WAL reaches the operating system but is not <code class="text-cyan-400">fsync</code>ed before the write returns. PostgreSQL's default (<code class="text-cyan-400">synchronous_commit=on</code>) flushes before commit returns, a stronger and much slower guarantee. So PostgreSQL runs with <code class="text-cyan-400">synchronous_commit=off</code>, the setting that matches what SoliDB promises: survive a process crash, not a power cut. Neither column is "durable writes".</p>
<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-8 mb-3">Create &mdash; one INSERT per request</h3>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 mb-6"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-300"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4">Stack</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">req/s</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">p99</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">CPU/req</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">vs Rails</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-gray-400 divide-y divide-white/10">
<tr class="bg-white/5"><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-bold">Soli</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-white">135,103</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-white">1.78 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-white">22 &micro;s (60 incl. SoliDB)</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-white">4.3&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Phoenix + Ecto + HEEx</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">124,305</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.65 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">114 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.9&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Express + EJS + Sequelize</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">91,537</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.45 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">162 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">2.9&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">AdonisJS + Lucid + Edge</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">53,772</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">6.83 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">282 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.7&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Rails + Puma</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">31,778</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">12.92 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">473 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.0&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">FastAPI + SQLAlchemy + Jinja2</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">29,035</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">20.69 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">526 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.9&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Django + gunicorn</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">19,957</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">22.19 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">459 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.6&times;</td></tr>
<tr class="text-gray-500"><td class="py-3 px-4">Laravel + Octane <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide">reference</span></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">13,175</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">16.88 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1,105 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.4&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Laravel + php-fpm</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">6,372</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">33.06 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">2,260 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.2&times;</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">Laravel's php-fpm cell returned <strong class="text-white">50 HTTP 500s out of 190,961 responses</strong> (0.03%). Neither php-fpm, nginx nor Laravel logged a cause; the figure is printed with the failures counted rather than re-run until clean. The delete run on the same stack, later, returned none.</p>
<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-8 mb-3">Update &mdash; one row by primary key</h3>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 mb-6"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-300"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4">Stack</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">req/s</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">p99</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">CPU/req</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">vs Rails</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-gray-400 divide-y divide-white/10">
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Phoenix + Ecto + HEEx</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">123,792</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.57 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">114 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.3&times;</td></tr>
<tr class="bg-white/5"><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-bold">Soli</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-white">120,551</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-white">2.30 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-white">22 &micro;s (74 incl. SoliDB)</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-white">3.2&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Express + EJS + Sequelize</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">85,882</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.83 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">173 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">2.3&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">AdonisJS + Lucid + Edge</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">58,444</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">6.36 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">259 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.6&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Rails + Puma</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">37,502</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">12.29 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">394 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.0&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">FastAPI + SQLAlchemy + Jinja2</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">27,576</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">20.27 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">555 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.7&times;</td></tr>
